premise checks : REQUESTED POINT IS INADMISSIBLE - no modulus/density is reported at it.
   (1) eta = 1.02 is not a wall ratio: eta = r_inner/r_outer must lie in [0,1). eta >= 1 means the cavity is larger than the particle, i.e. negative wall volume and negative particle mass. If 1.02 was meant as an outer/inner radius ratio, the corresponding eta would be 1/1.02 = 0.9804, a shell of ~2% wall thickness that no commercial microballoon has - and it is in any case inconsistent with the K46 grade, whose datasheet true density fixes eta.
   (2) vf = 0.75 is not realisable for MONODISPERSE spheres: random close packing is 0.64 and even the densest ordered (FCC/HCP) packing of equal spheres is 0.7405 < 0.75. Above ~0.55 a real syntactic foam needs a polydisperse balloon size distribution (or deliberate particle deformation/crushing), which contradicts the stated 'monodisperse'.
